From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chelovechishee <261262090+chelovechishee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 28/52] soc: samsung: exynos-pmu: Exynos 7885 CPU power down
 for cpuidle

The EL3 monitor's PSCI CPU_SUSPEND only executes WFI; the PMU gates the
core when its CLUSTERx_CPUy_CONFIGURATION local power request is cleared
beforehand (downstream exynos-powermode cpu_disable()). A CPU PM notifier,
last in the chain, clears it on entry and sets it again on exit or a failed
entry, so a later plain WFI never powers the core down.

S-Boot leaves automatic cluster power down armed for the A73 and the second
A53 cluster: with both cores asleep the PMU cut the cluster with its L2,
never cleaned for a core-level request, and memory got corrupted. At init
every cluster sequencer is set to keep the cluster on (downstream
cluster_enable()).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
